cription of the Treasury's depositary system may be found in the Annual Report of the Secretary of the Treasury for 1955, pages 275-284.\nTable 1.- Status of the Account of the Treasurer of the United States\n(In millions of dollars)\n<table><tr><th rowspan=\"2\">End of fiscal year or month</th><th colspan=\"4\">Treasury operating balance</th><th colspan=\"4\">Assets</th><th rowspan=\"2\">Liabilities 1/</th><th rowspan=\"2\">Balance in account of Treasurer of U. S.</th></tr><tr><th>Arreivable funds in Federal Reserve Banks</th><th>Tax and loan accounts in special depositaries</th><th>Gold in Treasury fund</th><th>Total operating balance</th><th>Silver, coin, and currency</th><th>Unclassified collections, etc.</th><th>In Federal Reserve Banks in process of collection</th><th>In other depositaries</th><th>Total assets</th></tr><tr><td>1950</td><td>950</td><td>3,268</td><td>1,052</td><td>5,269</td><td>191</td><td>20</td><td>143</td><td>303</td><td>5,927</td><td>410</td><td>5,517</td></tr><tr><td>1951</td><td>338</td><td>5,680</td><td>1,046</td><td>7,064</td><td>176</td><td>24</td><td>250</td><td>356</td><td>7,871</td><td>514</td><td>7,357</td></tr><tr><td>1952</td><td>333</td><td>5,106</td><td>1,009</td><td>6,448</td><td>194</td><td>34</td><td>355</td><td>450</td><td>7,481</td><td>512</td><td>6,969</td></tr><tr><td>1953</td><td>132</td><td>3,071</td><td>984</td><td>4,187</td><td>161</td><td>75</td><td>210</td><td>463</td><td>5,096</td><td>426</td><td>4,670</td></tr><tr><td>1954</td><td>875</td><td>4,836</td><td>497</td><td>6,207</td><td>191</td><td>50</td><td>274</td><td>520</td><td>7,243</td><td>476</td><td>6,766</td></tr><tr><td>1955</td><td>380</td><td>4,359</td><td>493</td><td>5,213</td><td>197</td><td>93</td><td>343</td><td>500</td><td>6,362</td><td>146 2/</td><td>6,216</td></tr><tr><td>1956</td><td>282</td><td>4,631</td><td>501</td><td>5,656</td><td>159</td><td>37</td><td>421</td><td>438</td><td>6,712</td><td>156</td><td>6,546</td></tr><tr><td>1957</td><td>498</t